│ ┃  Patch to Resolve Enumeration Type Usage in Django Templates   ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue arises because YearInSchool is a class and not a simple  │
│ enum type, which causes Django templates to call it as a callable  │
│ with no arguments. To resolve this, we add a                       │
│ do_not_call_in_templates = True attribute to the Choices class,    │
│ which is the parent of YearInSchool. This allows Django to treat   │
│ Choices as a non-callable type when used in templates.             │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│ [file]utils/choices.py[/file] [original]class Choices:[/original]  │
