│    listed (e.g., utils/choices.py or another module).              │
│  • The Choices class is defined in                                 │
│    django/db/models/fields/choices.py or another location.         │
│  • The do_not_call_in_templates method is not present in the       │
│    Choices class, which is critical for disabling callable         │
│    behavior in templates.                                          │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                        📌 2. Bug Locations                         │
│                                                                    │
│ Location 1:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • File: utils/choices.py                                          │
│  • Class: YearInSchool                                             │
│  • Intended Behavior: The YearInSchool class should be a static    │
│    enumeration type (e.g., YearInSchool.FRESHMAN as a constant)    │
│    rather than a callable class.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ Location 2:                                                        │
│                                                                    │
│  • File: django/db/models/fields/choices.py                        │
│  • Class: Choices                                                  │
│  • Intended Behavior: The do_not_call_in_templates method should   │
│    be added to the Choices class to disable callable behavior in   │
│    Django templates.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                           🛠️ Intended Fix                           │
│                                                                    │
│ To resolve the issue, the do_not_call_in_templates method must be  │
│ added to the Choices class in django/db/models/fields/choices.py.  │
│ This method would prevent the class from being callable in         │
│ templates, allowing enumeration types like YearInSchool to be used │
│ directly in templates without errors.                              │
│                                                                    │
│ Example Fix (pseudo-code):                                         │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  # Add the method to Choices                                       │
│  class Choices:                                                    │
│      @classmethod                                                  │
│      def do_not_call_in_templates(cls):                            │
│          # Implementation to disable callable behavior             │
│          pass                                                      │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ This ensures that Django templates can use YearInSchool.FRESHMAN   │
│ without requiring arguments.                                       │
